@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

title Cache Put / Populate Flow (full-p2p)

participant "Client\n(Python/shmq)" as client
participant "Shmq Mailbox\n(/dev/shm)" as shmq
participant "DispatcherP2p" as disp
participant "MemoryTier\n(DRAM pool)" as mt
participant "DispatchMap" as dm
participant "BackgroundWriter" as bgw
participant "ExtentManager" as em
participant "BlockDevice\n(NVMe SSD)" as ssd

note over disp: Put path is identical to the `full` profile.\nThe P2P BAR1 ring only affects the cold READ path.

== Synchronous Path (client-visible) ==

client -> shmq: BatchPopulateRequest\n(key, IpcHandle)
shmq -> shmq: cudaIpcOpenMemHandle\n-> device_ptr
shmq -> disp: populate(key, IpcHandle)

disp -> mt: evict_lru() if pool full
note right of mt: LRU entries with\ncompleted write-through\nare eligible

disp -> mt: reserve_memory(key, size)\n-> mem_ptr
note right of mt: First-fit alloc from\nmmap'd CUDA-pinned pool

disp -> disp: copy_gpu_to_memory_async\n(GPU -> mem_ptr, store stream)
note right of disp: Async D2H into\npinned memory-tier slot

disp -> dm: copy_gpu_to_memory_completed\n-> create_memory_tier_entry(key, ptr, size)
note right of dm: Entry visible to\ncheck/lookup immediately

disp -> dm: downgrade_reference\n(write -> read)

disp --> shmq: Ok
shmq -> shmq: cudaIpcCloseMemHandle
shmq --> client: BatchPopulateResponse\n(success)

== Asynchronous Write-Through ==

disp -> bgw: enqueue WriteJob\n(key, size, drive_idx)
bgw -> mt: get(key) -> (ptr, size)
bgw -> em: reserve_extent(key, size)\n-> WriteHandle
bgw -> ssd: write segments\n(MDTS-aware chunked I/O)
note right of ssd: Split into max_transfer_size\nchunks, each via WriteSync

bgw -> em: publish()\n(finalize extent)
bgw -> dm: convert_to_storage\n(key, block_offset)
note right of dm: ssd_offset set; entry stays\nMemoryTier, now durable/evictable

bgw -> dm: release_read(key)

note over mt, ssd: Entry exists in BOTH DRAM and SSD.\nLookups served from DRAM (warm).\nIf evicted from DRAM -> served over P2P cold path (SSD -> BAR1 -> GPU).

@enduml
